<p class="eyebrow">DEMAND VALIDATION · PRIVATE</p><h1>What people want to discover.</h1><div class="admin-stats"><div class="admin-stat"><strong><%= @total %></strong><span>Active waitlist signups</span></div><div class="admin-stat"><strong><%= @confirmed %></strong><span>Email-confirmed signups</span></div><div class="admin-stat"><strong><%= Product.where(selected_for_first_import: true).count %></strong><span>Selected for first import</span></div></div>
<h2>Signups over time</h2><% if @days.any? %><div class="bar-chart"><% @days.last(60).each do |day,count| %><div class="bar-column"><span style="height:<%= [count * 110.0 / @days.values.max, 3].max.round %>px" title="<%= day %>: <%= count %>"></span><div><%= count %></div><small><%= day.strftime('%d/%m') %></small></div><% end %></div><% else %><p class="admin-empty">No signups yet. Real data will appear here.</p><% end %>
<div class="admin-columns"><section><h2>Countries</h2><%= render 'admin/shared/counts', counts: @countries, label: 'Country' %></section><section><h2>France · postcodes</h2><%= render 'admin/shared/counts', counts: @postcodes, label: 'Postcode' %></section></div>
<h2>Product demand</h2><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Product</th><th>All interest signals</th><th>Confirmed subscribers</th><th>First import</th></tr></thead><tbody><% @products.sort_by { |p| -(@confirmed_interest[p.id] || 0) }.each do |product| %><tr><td><%= link_to product.name, edit_admin_product_path(product) %></td><td><%= @interest[product.id] || 0 %></td><td><%= @confirmed_interest[product.id] || 0 %></td><td><%= product.selected_for_first_import? ? 'Selected' : '—' %></td></tr><% end %></tbody></table></div><p class="tiny muted">Anonymous signals are deduplicated within the visitor’s preference session. They are weaker evidence than email-confirmed interest. No counts are fabricated.</p>
<h2>Requested categories</h2><%= render 'admin/shared/counts', counts: @categories, label: 'Category (unique active subscribers, explicit + product favourites)' %>
<h2>Acquisition</h2><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>UTM source</th><th>Medium</th><th>Campaign</th><th>Content</th><th>Active signups</th></tr></thead><tbody><% @acquisition.sort_by { |_,count| -count }.each do |keys,count| %><tr><% keys.each do |key| %><td><%= key.presence || 'Direct / unspecified' %></td><% end %><td><%= count %></td></tr><% end %></tbody></table></div>
<h2>Page views → confirmed signups</h2><p class="admin-note">Directional only: aggregate requests, not unique people. Bots, repeat visits and time-to-confirm affect this ratio. Attribution follows a signed landing context for up to two hours, without an analytics identifier or marketing cookie.</p><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Landing page</th><th>Aggregate views</th><th>Confirmed signups attributed</th><th>Signup / view ratio</th></tr></thead><tbody><% @views.sort_by { |_,n| -n }.each do |path,views| %><tr><td><%= path %></td><td><%= views %></td><td><%= @conversions[path] || 0 %></td><td><%= number_to_percentage(100.0 * (@conversions[path] || 0) / views, precision: 1) %></td></tr><% end %></tbody></table></div>
